Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: navy cards and a cyan focus ring in setup

Setup design (sable-setup-wizard-titan2): content sits on navy cards
and the focused control has a cyan ring.

Resources: @drawable/sable_setup_card (fill, 1dp stroke, 14dp corners)
and @drawable/sable_setup_focus_ring (a 3dp outline drawn only in the
focused state), with their colours in @color/sable_setup_card,
sable_setup_card_stroke and sable_setup_focus. The defaults here follow
the platform palette (system_neutral2 / system_accent1, light and
night); SableSetupWizardOverlay sets the Sable navy and cyan values.

The SableSetupCard style puts the Privacy paragraphs on cards; the
Keyboard status and the Theme step's Sable accent line use the same
card.

sable/SableFocusRing gives every view that takes focus in a step, and
has no foreground of its own, the ring as its foreground, so it shows
on Glif buttons, radio buttons, text fields and Sable links alike and
replaces the platform's grey focus highlight. Lists keep their row
highlight. Any failure leaves the platform highlight.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
